    "result_text": "The full suite is that single `AcceptanceTest` (the other two test files are the abstract base and a helper), and it's green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change makes owner creation return `displayName` formatted as `'LastName, FirstName'`.\n\nTwo files touched, both minimal:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `displayName` string to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains a `displayName` field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Person.java`** \u2014 added a `getDisplayName()` deriving `lastName + \", \" + firstName` from the stored names.\n\nMapStruct maps by property name, so `getDisplayName()` is auto-wired into `OwnerDto.setDisplayName` with **no change to `OwnerMapper` or any controller**.\n\n**Structural-impact reasoning:** I put the new getter on `Person`, a tiny class (only four CC-1 accessors, so `WMC_other` \u2248 4) rather than on `Owner` (large `getPet`-heavy class with high `WMC_other`) or in the mapper interface. The new method is CC 1, and no existing method body was modified \u2014 so every changed function stays simple and the whole class it lives in is cheap to hold in context.",
